# Client Brief

## Background

United Amara Bank (UAB) publishes annual financial reports containing detailed financial information. However, management requires a more interactive way to monitor performance trends, compare reporting periods and communicate insights efficiently.

## Problem Statement

Financial information is presented in static reports, making it time-consuming to compare performance, identify trends and support executive decision-making. Management needs a consolidated view of financial performance, balance-sheet growth, profitability and financial resilience.

## Project Objective

Develop an Executive Financial Performance Dashboard in Power BI using UAB Bank's published financial statements to support evidence-based decision-making.

## Scope

The dashboard analyses:

- Financial Position
- Financial Performance
- Profitability
- Asset Quality
- Liquidity
- Key Banking KPIs

Key metrics include:

- Total Assets
- Customer Deposits
- Customer Loans
- Operating Income
- Operating Expenses
- Profit After Tax
- ROAA
- ROAE
- Gross NPL Ratio
- Loan Loss Coverage
- Liquidity Ratio

## Expected Outcome

The dashboard will enable executives to:

- Monitor financial performance
- Identify long-term trends
- Evaluate profitability
- Assess asset quality
- Monitor liquidity and financial resilience
- Identify potential management risks
- Support strategic planning and evidence-based decision-making